From: app_manager
Subject: [PATCH] Inject engine-initialization trace into the script runtime

Adds a loud stdout marker when the Servo script runtime initializes, so a
minimal/custom build can confirm the engine booted. Anchored on
Runtime::new_with_parent, which is the stable init entry point in current
Servo (the old `pub fn init` no longer exists).

If this patch stops applying after a Servo tree update, the drift is real:
resolve it manually instead of suppressing the failure.

 components/script/script_runtime.rs | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/components/script/script_runtime.rs b/components/script/script_runtime.rs
--- a/components/script/script_runtime.rs
+++ b/components/script/script_runtime.rs
@@ -771,5 +771,8 @@ impl Runtime {
     pub(crate) unsafe fn new_with_parent(
         parent: Option<ParentRuntime>,
         script_event_loop_sender: Option<ScriptEventLoopSender>,
     ) -> Runtime {
+        println!("=========================================");
+        println!("[ENGINE ROOT HACKED] Native Rust core initialization successful!");
+        println!("=========================================");
         let mut runtime = if let Some(parent) = parent {
